              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JAJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made snow ice cream with my mom's recipe for 50 years. This recipe called for half and half and vanilla extract, plus sugar to taste. It never had any amounts of anything - you just keep adding ingredients until it is \"perfect\". The deciding factor is to only use the driest, fluffiest snow you can find. Wet snow does not let the magic work!",
            "datePublished": "2022-07-01T01:57:54.144Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "carahafen7"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Sometimes it just isn't worth making and this recipe falls into that category. I found it to be sickeningly sweet. I know that I could fiddle around with the sugar and vanilla amounts, but as is I would never make this recipe again.",
